            "created": "2026-10-16T13:44:12.301942Z",
            "modified": "2026-10-16T13:44:12.301942Z",
            "name": "Ransomware File Encryption Pattern (.locked)",
            "description": "Detects files being renamed with a '.locked' extension, a common indicator of ransomware activity mentioned in the cyber observables.",
            "indicator_types": [
                "malicious-activity"
            ],
            "pattern": "title: Ransomware File Encryption with .locked Extension\nid: 2b9a7c3d-1e8f-4b9a-8c7d-6e5f4d3c2b1a\nstatus: experimental\ndescription: Detects the creation of files with a '.locked' extension, a common pattern for ransomware observed in attacks in Japan.\nreferences:\n  - https://www.cpomagazine.com/cyber-security/string-of-ransomware-cyber-attacks-prompts-first-cybersecurity-state-of-emergency-declaration-from-japan/\nauthor: cyber.netsecops.io\ndate: 2026-10-16\ntags:\n  - attack.t1486\n  - attack.impact\nfalsepositives:\n  - Legitimate applications that may use this extension for lock files, though uncommon as a final file extension.\nlevel: high\nlogsource:\n  category: file_event\n  product: windows\ndetection:\n  selection:\n    TargetFilename|endswith: '.locked'\n  condition: selection",
            "pattern_type": "sigma",
            "valid_from": "2026-10-16T13:44:12.074601Z"
        },
