            "created": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
            "modified": "2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z",
            "name": "Japan Declares First-Ever Cybersecurity State of Emergency",
            "description": "## Executive Summary\n\nIn an unprecedented response to a wave of crippling cyberattacks, the **Japanese government** has declared its first-ever **\"cybersecurity state of emergency.\"** The decision, made by the National Cybersecurity Strategy Headquarters (NCSH), comes after a series of devastating ransomware and data breach incidents in September and October 2026. These attacks have impacted nearly 500 companies and exposed the personal information of an estimated **14 million citizens**. A large-scale ransomware attack on cloud services provider **IDC Frontier** (owned by SoftBank) acted as a tipping point, causing a supply chain-style compromise of 495 downstream businesses. Officials attribute the surge in successful attacks to threat actors using AI-driven tools to bypass the",
            "report_types": [
                "threat-report"
            ],
            "published": "2026-10-16T00:00:00Z",
